{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"reversed","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ReversedCollection","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/ReversedCollection","preciseIdentifier":"s:s18ReversedCollectionV"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"discussion","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"You can reverse a collection without allocating new space for its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"elements by calling this ","type":"text"},{"code":"reversed()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" method. A ","type":"text"},{"code":"ReversedCollection","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"instance wraps an underlying collection and provides access to its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"elements in reverse order. This example prints the characters of a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"string in reverse order:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let word = \"Backwards\"","for char in word.reversed() {","    print(char, terminator: \"\")","}","\/\/ Prints \"sdrawkcaB\""],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"If you need a reversed collection of the same type, you may be able to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"use the collection’s sequence-based or collection-based initializer. For","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"example, to get the reversed version of a string, reverse its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"characters and initialize a new ","type":"text"},{"code":"String","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" instance from the result.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let reversedWord = String(word.reversed())","print(reversedWord)","\/\/ Prints \"sdrawkcaB\""],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"style":"note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"O(1)"}]}],"name":"Complexity","type":"aside"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Unicode\/Scalar\/UTF16View\/reversed()","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"title":"reversed()","externalID":"s:SKsE8reverseds18ReversedCollectionVyxGyF::SYNTHESIZED::s:s7UnicodeO6ScalarV9UTF16ViewV","symbolKind":"method","platforms":[{"deprecated":false,"unavailable":false,"name":"iOS","beta":false,"introducedAt":"8.0"},{"unavailable":false,"name":"iPadOS","introducedAt":"8.0","deprecated":false,"beta":false},{"deprecated":false,"unavailable":false,"name":"Mac Catalyst","beta":false,"introducedAt":"13.0"},{"unavailable":false,"name":"macOS","introducedAt":"10.10","deprecated":false,"beta":false},{"unavailable":false,"name":"tvOS","introducedAt":"9.0","deprecated":false,"beta":false},{"unavailable":false,"name":"visionOS","introducedAt":"1.0","deprecated":false,"beta":false},{"unavailable":false,"name":"watchOS","introducedAt":"2.0","deprecated":false,"beta":false}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"reversed"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"ReversedCollection","preciseIdentifier":"s:s18ReversedCollectionV"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"roleHeading":"Instance Method","extendedModule":"Swift","modules":[{"name":"Swift"}],"role":"symbol"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Unicode","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Unicode\/Scalar","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Unicode\/Scal